; Appended after circle.horn.
; Closed-term weakening. A term with no free variables and no free
; dimensions that is typed (or equated) in the empty context, with no
; dimensions and the true face, keeps its typing in every well-formed
; restricted context: weakening by variables and dimensions and restriction
; to a face are admissible for every rule, and this states their composite
; for closed terms. It lets a closed library term (ua, iso-equiv, an
; equivalence) be checked once, instead of once per context it occurs in.
(rule rhas.closed ((rhas z nil ft ?t ?a) (scoped z z ?t) (rctx ?d ?g ?phi))
  (rhas ?d ?g ?phi ?t ?a))
(rule req.closed ((req z nil ft ?t ?s ?a) (scoped z z ?t) (scoped z z ?s)
    (rctx ?d ?g ?phi))
  (req ?d ?g ?phi ?t ?s ?a))
